 \"url\": \"https://brightluxx.com\", \"logo\": \"https://files.ihgbrands.com/uploads_hero_banner.webp\"}, \"url\": \"https://brightluxx.com/products/bl-sph300\"}, \"additionalProperty\": [{\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Pixel Pitch\", \"value\": \"3.0mm\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Brightness\", \"value\": \"1,200 nits\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Resolution\", \"value\": \"Custom per sphere size\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Warranty\", \"value\": \"3 Years Standard | 5 Years Extended Available\"}]}10:Tb60,{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the pixel pitch of SphereVision 3mm and why is it important?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The SphereVision 3mm has a 3.0mm pixel pitch, meaning pixels are spaced 3mm apart. This allows for high-resolution content, ideal for close viewing in spaces like museums and lobbies where image clarity is critical.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How is the SphereVision 3mm installed and what mounting options are available?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"It supports both ceiling and floor stand mounting, providing flexible installation options based on your venue requirements. The modular design eases assembly into seamless spheres ranging from 1 to 5 meters in diameter.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What kind of warranty do you offer for the SphereVision 3mm?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"We provide a standard industry warranty that covers manufacturing defects and performance issues. Specific terms can vary, so we recommend contacting our sales team for detailed warranty information tailored to your project.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How does the SphereVision 3mm compare to flat LED displays?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Unlike flat displays, SphereVision 3mm offers a full 360-degree spherical viewing experience with triangular tessellation for seamless content wrap. This makes it ideal for immersive storytelling environments not possible with traditional flat screens.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the typical power consumption of this product?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"On average, the SphereVision 3mm consumes 300W per square meter, balancing bright visuals at 1,200 nits while maintaining energy efficiency suitable for extended use in public spaces.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can the SphereVision 3mm handle real-time content updates?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes, it includes real-time mapping software enabling dynamic 360-degree content playback. This makes it perfect for exhibitions, events, and planetariums needing live or frequently changing content.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the size range available for the SphereVision 3mm?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"SphereVision 3mm modules tessellate to form spheres from 1 meter up to 5 meters in diameter, allowing customization for different spatial and design requirements.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is SphereVision 3mm suitable for outdoor use?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"SphereVision 3mm is primarily designed for indoor environments such as museums and lobbies due to its brightness of 1,200 nits. For outdoor applications, higher brightness and different protective measures may be needed.\"}}]}5:[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"data-testid\":\"next-server-rendered-parity-page\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"script\",\"0\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$f\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",\"1\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$10\"}}],\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\"],\"$L14\"]}]\n11:[\"